    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5490" root="جرد" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُجَرَّدٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُرْدَةٌ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  (tropical:)  A <i>bare,</i>
or <i>naked,</i> [or <i>drawn,</i>] sword. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [ (assumed tropical:)  <i>Divested
of every accessory, adjunct, appendage,</i> or <i>adventitious thing; rendered bare, shere,</i> or <i>mere;
abstract.</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  In philosophy, <i>Bodiless; incorporeal; as though divested of body.</i>] ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الجُرْدَانُ</span>.

